<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17178" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-scrĕo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">excr-</span></b> ), āre, v.
		a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
			hawk</i> or <i>cough up</i>, <i>to spit
				out by coughing</i>: per tussim exscreatur, si tolerabilis
			morbus est, pituita; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si gravis, sanguis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
					6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					24, 16, 92, § 145</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">age, age, usque excrea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 1, 1, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numquam exscreare ausus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 21, 24</span></i>.</div>
